    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe locality derivation now prefers the postcode over the city.\n\n**`model/Locality.java`** \u2014 added a two-argument `of(String city, String postcode)` that:\n1. Looks up the region by postcode range first (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) via a new private `fromPostcode` helper.\n2. Falls back to the existing city-to-region table only when the postcode is null, malformed, or in no known range.\n\nThe original single-argument `of(String city)` is retained unchanged, so `Postcode.isValidForCity` (which validates a postcode against the *city's* region) keeps its city-based semantics.\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `locality` mapping now calls `Locality.of(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode())`.\n\nResult:\n- Known cities with in-range postcodes still yield the same region (`coreRegionFromPostcodeRange`: Sydney/2000 \u2192 NSW).\n- Cities that share a name are disambiguated by postcode (`functionalityPostcodePreferredOverCity`: unknown city with postcode 3000 \u2192 VIC).\n\nTests: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
