    "probe_text": "Reading the pipeline in `owners.POST.yml` and each function class, here is everything that happens for `POST /api/owners`, in order. Every step runs inside one shared `transaction` governance, so all writes commit once at the very end (or roll back if any step throws).\n\n## 0. Authorization (gate)\n`composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` \u2014 the whole endpoint is guarded; a caller without that role never reaches the pipeline.\n\n## 1. `ValidateOwnerFields` \u2014 field validation & normalization (throws \u2192 **400**)\nReads the `@RequestBody` once, collects *all* errors, and throws `OwnerFieldsInvalidException` if any exist:\n- **Required, non-blank:** `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`.\n- **Address (required):** normalized via `AddressNormalizer` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). Blank after normalization \u2192 error; otherwise the canonical form is written back onto the request.\n- **Telephone:** normalized to E.164 via `TelephoneE164` (strip spaces/dashes/brackets; assume `+61` and drop a leading `0` if no `+`; enforce 8\u201315 digits, and exact national length for `+61`=9 / `+1`=10). Invalid \u2192 error; valid \u2192 written back.\n- **Email (optional):** if present, must match the email regex; valid \u2192 stored trimmed + lower-cased; invalid \u2192 error.\n- **Postcode (optional):** if present, must be 4 digits and in-range for the city's region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown city accepts any 4 digits) via `Postcode.isValidForCity`; valid \u2192 stored trimmed; invalid \u2192 error.\n- **Side effect:** republishes the validated/normalized request as a variable for later steps.\n\n## 2. `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` \u2014 (throws \u2192 **409**)\nCounts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed). If \u2265 **50**, throws `OwnerCityAtCapacityException`.\n\n## 3. `CheckOwnerDailyLimit` \u2014 (throws \u2192 **429**)\nComputes the effective registration date (supplied, else today), rolls it to a business day (`BusinessDay.adjust` \u2014 weekend \u2192 next Monday), and counts existing owners registered on that day. If \u2265 **100**, throws `OwnerDailyLimitExceededException`.\n\n## 4. `BuildOwner` \u2014 construct entity\nMaps the DTO to an `Owner` via `OwnerMapper`, then sets `registrationDate` to the business-day-adjusted effective date (supplied or today). Publishes the `Owner`.\n\n## 5. `AssignHousehold` \u2014 side effect (conditional)\nOnly if `sharesHousehold` is true: finds existing owners with the same normalized lastName + address; reuses their `householdId` or derives a stable SHA-256-based `HH-...` id; sets it on the new owner and **back-fills + saves** existing housemates that lack it.\n\n## 6. `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` \u2014 duplicate check (throws \u2192 **409**)\nBuilds the `identityKey` = `normalizedTelephone | email | householdId` and, if any existing owner has the same whole key, throws `OwnerIdentityConflictException`.\n\n## 7. `AssignHouseholdSize` \u2014 derived field\nSets `householdSize` = existing owners sharing the `householdId` + 1 (1 if no household).\n\n## 8. `AssignCustomerCode` \u2014 derived field\nSets `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN is one more than the count of existing owners in that city (city compared case-insensitively).\n\n## 9. `AssignNamesakeCount` \u2014 derived field\nSets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with the same firstName + lastName (case-insensitive), excluding this one.\n\n## 10. `AssignBulkSignupWarning` \u2014 derived field\nSets `bulkSignupWarning` = true if more than **80** existing owners already share this owner's registration business day.\n\n## 11. `SaveOwner` \u2014 persist\n`ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 assigns the generated id.\n\n## 12. `AuditOwnerCreated` \u2014 side effect\nLogs on the `AUDIT` logger: id, customerCode, registrationDate, and derived `MembershipLevel` (base 1; +1 if email present; +1 if namesakeCount == 0; capped at 3).\n\n## 13. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` \u2014 response\nMaps to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`. The transaction commits here.\n\n---\n\n**Note on ordering:** the three rejection checks (fields \u2192 400, city capacity \u2192 409, daily limit \u2192 429) all run *before* `BuildOwner`/`SaveOwner`, so a rejected request never persists a record. Identity-uniqueness (\u2192 409) runs after household assignment so the `householdId` is part of the key \u2014 but note step 5 (`AssignHousehold`) can still have saved back-filled `householdId`s onto existing housemates; if a later step throws, that write rolls back with the shared transaction."
